<description>&lt;p&gt;Colombia opened an embassy in Jerusalem while UN independent experts urged Ecopetrol to provide reparations to armed-conflict victims and the UN Security Council heard calls for the peace deal to endure as insecurity grows. Opposition groups protested budget cuts that threaten the peace court and searches for the disappeared, and the peace tribunal charged former FARC members with anti-Indigenous crimes. Rebels detonated a car bomb outside a toll booth in Cauca, FARC dissidents were killed in a Catatumbo operation, and an army airstrike hit a teenager. 225 battle-related deaths were recorded in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.un.org/feed/view/en/story/2026/10/1168580&quot;&gt;UN News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiuAFBVV95cUxObUVqdXVtVUFCMDgyZ3c2dVptc2dndnQzTjdIRE9VLUM3MXMySDlfY2FqQkFfbmZyVGI2WkZIc0VyN2VmSTF1TEVqYXdNTEY4TDU2MHRlajlxem1mX29ta1p4NW1jUnBsZUQ4UjkyN1hPaWpzekpiYzV1bldQTi0tT1h3MVdLd28tR1FSY0pXVE9mTnV1WGlxNzlVM0lDLVdhYW5uQjhpckE1aVBoZ0hNb3hJLUlMdjZs?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiggFBVV95cUxNekpGdG9yb3JEZWVMa2lGT0NpTExVdGxDSXlRR1JkOUR2aXlkSFpPY2gwekZPVVBYM0dtc3pJMkFzRmhIV0JFUUViUzFWQ2R3WEhGTlZYcDFHeXRtWUZUcDdyNHFvQ1VPbS14T0dXVFF6RWtZSGgta1VfVmRyX1ZubVJn?oc=5&quot;&gt;ColombiaOne.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMirgFBVV95cUxPTDJjTlFobGJCWTNLQkpRTE9RSXlXdTd2SUZOX09US1NPOWJaeDhMaXZxWnlsQ28tUlNfVURIQlk1a2JfYmQ2bnFndFAxYnJCeGdocm03R3Blckg0SUoyLVFKZlJqcXRSTERxWDlMT0hsLWJtN0M5TnJmYTlfYnVWbFNCdGtTS3NDQWRBSDR6bWlYejFhRDQxMFpUMHVIZXZCM1BpT0pEQksxbnNZNkE?oc=5&quot;&gt;The City Paper Bogotá&lt;/a&gt;, &l